{"shortDescription":"Basis bids for hard red winter (HRW) wheat were steady to stronger in the southern U.S. Plains on Friday as surging K.C. wheat futures spurred farmers to book forward sales of new-crop wheat, while sales of remaining old-crop wheat, harvested this year, remained thin, merchandisers said.Basis value…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Basis bids for hard red winter (HRW) wheat were steady to stronger in the southern U.S. Plains on Friday as surging K.C. wheat futures spurred farmers to book forward sales of new-crop wheat, while sales of remaining old-crop wheat, harvested this year, remained thin, merchandisers said."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The spot-market basis for wheat improved by 10 cents a bushel at Catoosa, Oklahoma, amid a lack of grain movement."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere in Oklahoma, a dealer reported buying \"quite a bit\" of new-crop wheat for harvest in 2027. Farmers will begin planting that crop in coming weeks but some were already selling part of their expected 2027 harvest, seizing on multi-year highs in the futures market, the dealer said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["All K.C. (0#KW:) and CBOT ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZW1!","text":"CBOT:ZW1!"}}," wheat futures set life-of-contract highs on Friday for a third straight day, driven up by war-related disruptions to Black Sea grain exports and speculative buying, traders said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["K.C. September HRW wheat futures (KWU26) settled up 24-1/4 cents, or 3.1%, at $8.27-3/4 a bushel, and December futures (KWZ26) ended up 22-1/4 cents, or 2.8%, at $8.44-1/4 a bushel."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The K.C. December futures contract (KWZ26) has risen about $1.20 a bushel, or 16.6%, so far this month."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":[